I'm gonna tag this up for discussion today. Based on the existence of #10689, I'm thinking that there are gonna be folks that don't want the tray icon even with quake mode. 

Though, it might make sense that they'd be better served by a combo of #9992 and creating another window that's "snapped to the top", but _isn't_ named "_quake". Though, that does seem like a lot of work, cause that's

```json
{
  "windows": {
    "not_quake": {
      "snapToSide": "top",
      "launchMode": "focus"
    }
  },
  "minimizeToTray": false,
  "actions": [
    { "keys": "win+`", "command": { "action": "globalSummon", "name": "not_quake", "dropdownDuration": 200 } }
  ],
  ...
}
```


THOUGH

if we make `minimizeToTray` affect the quake window too, then we'll immediately get rid of that behavior for quake. It'll default to false, so then even the quake window won't get it. 

So yea, I think I'm in favor of "quake mode ignores `minimizeToTray`, always, and if you want quake mode without minimizing to the tray, then do {the above}"

